# COSS customization agent

This project customizes COSS UI on top of the stock scaffold. Act as the **customization agent**: know what changed, keep the log current, and separate library defaults from local edits.

## Source of truth

| Resource | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| [COSS-CUSTOMIZATION-LOG.md](COSS-CUSTOMIZATION-LOG.md) | Human-readable log of all token + component diffs |
| Git commit `04292fa` | Stock COSS baseline (`feat: initial commit`, post `npx shadcn init @coss/style`) |
| [app/coss-default-preset.css](app/coss-default-preset.css) | Runtime snapshot of `04292fa` tokens |
| [app/globals.css](app/globals.css) | Custom tokens (`:root:not([data-ui-preset="coss-default"])`) |

## What is customized (today)

**Tokens (`app/globals.css`):** blue primary (was neutral), `neutral-50` page background (was white), stronger input/muted opacity, darker destructive, new outline tokens, sans default font (was mono on `<html>`).

**Components:**
- [components/ui/button.tsx](components/ui/button.tsx) — `primary-outline`, restyled `destructive-outline`, height scale
- Height scale on form controls (`toggle`, `input`, `select`, `number-field`, `otp-field`, `combobox`): desktop `sm`/`default`/`lg`/`xl` = 28 / 32 / **48** / **56** (stock `lg` was 36, Button `xl` was 40)

**All other `components/ui/*` primitives** match the scaffold unless the log says otherwise.

## Preset system

- **Custom** (default): your tokens in `globals.css`
- **COSS**: stock tokens via `data-ui-preset="coss-default"` + `coss-default-preset.css`
- Toggle in header or press `p`; light/dark is separate (`d`)
- Component file edits (e.g. button variants) are **not** reverted by the preset — only CSS tokens

## Agent workflow

When the user changes theme tokens, COSS primitives, or asks about stock vs custom behavior:

1. **Read** `COSS-CUSTOMIZATION-LOG.md` first.
2. **Diff** against baseline: `git diff 04292fa -- app/globals.css app/layout.tsx components/ui/`
3. **Update the log** if tokens or `components/ui/*` changed — tables, new tokens, restore commands.
4. **Update** `app/coss-default-preset.css` only if the stock baseline definition changes (not when adding custom tokens).
5. **Prefer** updating custom tokens in `globals.css` under `:root:not([data-ui-preset="coss-default"])` — do not put custom values in `coss-default-preset.css`.

## Restore commands (quick reference)

```bash
# Stock tokens
git show 04292fa:app/globals.css

# Stock button
git show 04292fa:components/ui/button.tsx

# Runtime compare
# Use COSS preset toggle in the app
```

## Out of scope

- Re-implementing the preset toggle unless broken
- Editing COSS monorepo / registry internals
- Treating app pages (`app/page.tsx`, dashboard, sidebar) as COSS library changes — log them separately if relevant
